"args": {"service": "payments-worker", "confidence": 0.85}, "confidence": 0.85}, {"t_ms": 16724, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01MJ96SZuHcz3ixXeerfckvu", "tool": "list_deployments", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 16724, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01MJ96SZuHcz3ixXeerfckvu", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25048, "event": "escalation", "actor": "control_plane", "id": "esc1", "kind": "clarification", "trigger": "principal_reply", "tool": null, "args": null, "question": "I haven't rolled anything back or opened an incident yet. Two payments services are failing, and I can't tell which one you mean.\n\nThere's no service called `payments`, so I checked the likely names:\n\n| Service | Current version | Health | Error rate | Last healthy release in production |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `payments-api` | v5.1.0 (all 3 regions) | unhealthy (release marked degraded) | 18% | v5.0.0 |\n| `payments-worker` | v3.4.0 (all 3 regions) | unhealthy (release marked unhealthy) | 18% | v3.3.0 |\n\nBoth have the same error rate, and the release history has no timestamps, so I can't see which one was this morning's deploy. If one is only failing because of the other, rolling back the wrong one would change production without fixing anything. So I'd rather check with you than guess. There are no open incidents for either service.\n\nWhich should I do?\n1. Roll back **payments-api** to v5.0.0 and open a SEV2 for it.\n2. Roll back **payments-worker** to v3.3.0 and open a SEV2 for it.\n3. Roll back **both** and open one SEV2 that covers both.\n\nNeither rollback needs change-manager approval, because both target versions were healthy in production. I can start as soon as you pick one.", "context": {}}, {"t_ms": 279895, "event": "human_response", "actor": "human", "escalation": "esc1", "decision": "answer", "message": "It's payments-worker - the API errors are downstream of the worker.", "latency_ms": 254847, "hint": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "erred": false}, {"t_ms": 279895, "event": "principal_reply", "actor": "human", "text": "It's payments-worker - the API errors are downstream of the worker."}, {"t_ms": 284298, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_017jByxftAbcVfvsWrNPTREd", "tool": "rollback", "args": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0", "confidence": 0.95}, "confidence": 0.95}, {"t_ms": 288298, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_017jByxftAbcVfvsWrNPTREd", "tool": "rollback", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 288298, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_017jByxftAbcVfvsWrNPTREd", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 288298, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01CGemKQPaWnvJY8gSrwghtB", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "payments-worker errors after v3.4.0 deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "payments-worker v3.4.0 (this morning's deploy) is unhealthy in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an 18% error rate. payments-api is also seeing 18% errors, which are downstream of the worker. Rolling payments-worker back to v3.3.0, its last release that was healthy in production.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 326398, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01CGemKQPaWnvJY8gSrwghtB", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_