nd open a SEV2 for it.\n2. Roll back **payments-worker** to v3.3.0 and open a SEV2 for it.\n3. Roll back **both** and open one SEV2 that covers both.\n\nNeither rollback needs change-manager approval, because both target versions were healthy in production. I can start as soon as you pick one.", "type": "text"}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017jByxftAbcVfvsWrNPTREd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01CGemKQPaWnvJY8gSrwghtB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker errors after v3.4.0 deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "payments-worker v3.4.0 (this morning's deploy) is unhealthy in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an 18% error rate. payments-api is also seeing 18% errors, which are downstream of the worker. Rolling payments-worker back to v3.3.0, its last release that was healthy in production.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01C3LQUiAHtb6WQBGBLkwkts", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Hqpqp6HRm5LaNG7zr8gZiC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 and opened the SEV2. The worker has recovered, but payments-api is still failing.\n\n- **Rollback:** payments-worker is on v3.3.0 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It now reports healthy, and its error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** (SEV2, payments-worker), which paged on-call. It records that v3.4.0 was the bad deploy, that payments-api is erroring as a knock-on effect, and that the worker was rolled back to v3.3.0.\n- **payments-api:** When I checked right after the rollback, it was still unhealthy on v5.1.0 with an 18% error rate. It may just need time to recover, for example while retries or queued work clear. But its own v5.1.0 release is also marked degraded, so it may have a separate problem.\n\nI haven't touched payments-api. If its errors don't drop over the next few minutes, I can roll it back to v5.0.0, its last healthy release, and add that to INC-0001. Just say the word.", "type": "text"}]}]}